<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Locarno</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Locarno is a town in the canton of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ticino">Ticino</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>, on the northern shore of Lake Maggiore. Ruled by the Swiss confederates from 1513, it expelled its Protestant community in 1555, and many of the exiles, including the Orelli and Muralt families, settled in Zürich, where they revived the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a> industry. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/locarno-treaties">Locarno Treaties</a> were negotiated there in 1925.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/locarno.jpg" alt="Locarno" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ozonski · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Locarno_porto_-_panoramio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
